[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2838695146","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105900#issuecomment-2838695146","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105900","id":2838695146,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pMwzq","user":{"login":"Arnklit","id":4955051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NTUwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4955051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit","html_url":"https://github.com/Arnklit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-29T12:45:41Z","updated_at":"2025-04-29T12:48:38Z","body":"> `String` has case insensitive comparison methods, so I'm not sure this is the best way to fix the issue. Especially since you might be copying quite a lot of data, making this potentially pretty slow!\r\n\r\nThe fuzzy functions rely on find_char which doesn't have the concept of case sensitivity as far as I can tell. So not really sure how to change this without making a version of the tokens that is lower case. I'd be quite interested to hear from @a-johnston or @samsface as I'm not super familiar with this code.\r\n\r\nEDIT: Note the tokens is just the search string chopped into pieces by spaces \" \", so it's not lot of data.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2838695146/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2839131152","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105900#issuecomment-2839131152","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105900","id":2839131152,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pObQQ","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-29T14:23:37Z","updated_at":"2025-04-29T14:40:27Z","body":"Good catch, `case_sensitive` wasn't tested on its own since there was only the one desired behavior for the initial use case, and the fact that it could do either case sensitive or insensitive gave some false confidence in coverage.\r\n\r\nI would recommend instead of this approach to make `case_sensitive` private, add an overload `FuzzySearch::set_query(const String &p_query, bool p_case_sensitive)`, and then change the original method to just call `set_query(p_query, !p_query.is_lowercase());`. This would avoid creating new token strings for every target string as well as remove other weirdness of being able to change case sensitivity during matching (for example with this change it would be possible to manually set `case_sensitive = false`, call `search`, change `case_sensitive = true`, and then have mutated tokens for future matching). However I just got up and haven't had coffee so maybe I'm overlooking something\r\n\r\nedit: Also if you're already going to be touching this code, `p_result(s)` should probably be `r_result(s)`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2839131152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2840556074","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105900#issuecomment-2840556074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105900","id":2840556074,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pT3Iq","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T00:57:22Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T00:57:22Z","body":"@Arnklit does the recommendation make sense? If you would prefer I can open a pr against your branch but I didn't want to clobber/redo anything you were working on","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2840556074/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841451913","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105900#issuecomment-2841451913","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105900","id":2841451913,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pXR2J","user":{"login":"Arnklit","id":4955051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NTUwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4955051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit","html_url":"https://github.com/Arnklit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T09:59:19Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T09:59:19Z","body":"@a-johnston feel free to just log a new PR that supersedes this one and I'll close this. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841451913/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842093569","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105900#issuecomment-2842093569","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105900","id":2842093569,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pZugB","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T14:01:51Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T14:01:51Z","body":"Does the case sensitivity need to be an option? \r\nIt could just be part of the scoring algorithm, so non-matching case gives less weight than matching case, but its not considered a miss.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842093569/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842964842","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105900#issuecomment-2842964842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105900","id":2842964842,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pdDNq","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T18:45:19Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T18:45:19Z","body":"> Does the case sensitivity need to be an option? It could just be part of the scoring algorithm, so non-matching case gives less weight than matching case, but its not considered a miss.\r\n\r\nMaybe. There is already a tie breaker for de-weighting matches that rely on case insensitivity and that could be a larger factor while not counting casing misses the same as letter misses but it would require re-tuning the scoring algo. Maybe a miss budget can be used instead of a miss count and have letter misses count more against a result than a casing miss (while also allowing more casing misses before a result is omitted. right now by default up to 2 misses are allowed).\r\n\r\nI personally like the current default behavior as it allows me to choose to be more precise by searching with capitalization, which helps quickly bubble up .cs scripts for example. But I don't think it would be needed if either of the above solutions worked well enough.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842964842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]